# CSS is owned by Stylelint, not Prettier. The styles were ported verbatim from
# the single-file build in a compact one-rule-per-line idiom; letting Prettier
# reformat them would explode ~1,100 lines and undo that. Keeping the two tools
# off each other's turf also stops them fighting over the same files.
*.css

# prettier-plugin-astro always splits a <span>…</span> <a>…</a> sibling pair
# onto separate lines, even when the source is already a tight one-liner that
# fits printWidth. Astro's compressHTML deletes newline-adjacent whitespace
# between sibling tags entirely (Global Constraint 12), so that reformat
# silently deletes the rendered space between "work" and "selected projects"
# (and the other contact-list rows) — a real, confirmed pixel regression, not
# a hypothetical one. The usual escape hatch, `<!-- prettier-ignore -->`, is
# not safe here either: it has a byte-offset/UTF-16 conversion bug in this
# plugin version that corrupts the following markup whenever a multi-byte
# character (em dash, accented letter, arrow glyph) appears anywhere earlier
# in the document — verified with a minimal repro — and both files are full of
# them. Excluding the two files is the only reformat-stable, pixel-safe
# option; hand-format them if they ever need to change.
src/pages/404.astro
src/pages/contact.astro
